1. Using the app. You may download the official releases of RSL Companion Account Data Extractor
   (from this repository's GitHub Releases or from rslcompanion.com) and run them on your own
   computer to send your own game account's data to RSL Companion.

2. Reading the code. You may read the source on GitHub, and you may fork it on GitHub only to the
   extent GitHub's Terms of Service require. A fork grants no further rights.

3. Data files. The game-memory maps and offsets this software ships, downloads or produces (including
   known-offsets.json, calibrated-offsets.json, offsets_cache.json and the responses of the RSL Companion
   memory-map service), the export schemas and the metadata files in this repository are part of this
   software. You may not extract, copy or reuse them, in whole or in part, in any other software, tool,
   service or dataset.

4. No reverse engineering. You may not decompile, disassemble or otherwise reverse engineer the app or
   the extraction engine it contains, except where applicable law expressly permits it despite this
   restriction.

